{"name":"Valerian","hex":"#9f7a93","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Valerian","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["a Roman cognomen, notably borne by Publius Licinius Valerianus, a Roman emperor","A male given name from Latin, of rare usage."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A transliteration of the Russian male given name Валериа́н (Valerián)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Valerian"}],"entries":[{"title":"Valérian and Laureline","blocks":[{"text":"Valérian and Laureline, originally titled Valérian: Spatio-Temporal Agent and also commonly known as Valérian, is a French science fiction comics series, created by writer Pierre Christin and artist Jean-Claude Mézières. It was first published in Pilote magazine in 1967; the final installment was published in 2010. All of the Valérian stories have been collected in comic album format, comprising some twenty-one volumes plus a short story collection and an encyclopedia."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/ea/Valerian_and_Laureline-comics_album_21.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Val%C3%A9rian_and_Laureline"},{"title":"Valerian and the City of a Thousand Planets","blocks":[{"text":"Valerian and the City of a Thousand Planets is a 2017 space opera film written and directed by Luc Besson, and produced by his wife, Virginie Besson-Silla. It is based on the French science fiction comics series Valérian and Laureline, written by Pierre Christin, illustrated by Jean-Claude Mézières, and published by Dargaud. It stars Dane DeHaan and Cara Delevingne as Valerian and Laureline, respectively, with Clive Owen, Rihanna, Ethan Hawke, Herbie Hancock, Kris Wu and Rutger Hauer in supporting roles. Besson independently financed and personally funded the film. With a production budget of around $180 million, it is both the most expensive European and the most expensive independent film ever made. The film is a large international co-production between France, the United States, China, Germany, Belgium, and the United Arab Emirates."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/07/Valerian_and_the_City_of_a_Thousand_Planets.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valerian_and_the_City_of_a_Thousand_Planets"},{"title":"Valerian (herb)","blocks":[{"text":"Valerian is an herbaceous perennial flowering plant in the family Caprifoliaceae, native to Europe and southwestern Asia. It is the type species of the genus Valeriana."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Valeriana_officinalis_inflorescence_-_Niitv%C3%A4lja.jpg/330px-Valeriana_officinalis_inflorescence_-_Niitv%C3%A4lja.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valerian_(herb)"},{"title":"Valerian (emperor)","blocks":[{"text":"Valerian was Roman emperor from 253 to spring 260 AD. He rose to power during a particularly unstable period during the Crisis of the Third Century and appointed his son Gallienus as co-emperor."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Valerianus_Ny_Carlsberg_Glyptotek_IN3387.jpg/330px-Valerianus_Ny_Carlsberg_Glyptotek_IN3387.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valerian_(emperor)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/M%C3%A9zi%C3%A8res_-_Christin_-_Tranl%C3%A9.jpg/500px-M%C3%A9zi%C3%A8res_-_Christin_-_Tranl%C3%A9.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/M%C3%A9zi%C3%A8res_-_Christin_-_Tranl%C3%A9.jpg/1280px-M%C3%A9zi%C3%A8res_-_Christin_-_Tranl%C3%A9.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/M%C3%A9zi%C3%A8res_-_Christin_-_Tranl%C3%A9.jpg/500px-M%C3%A9zi%C3%A8res_-_Christin_-_Tranl%C3%A9.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Creators of Valérian and Laureline: Eveline Tranlé (colorist), Pierre Christin (writer), Jean-Claude Mézières (illustrator)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AM%C3%A9zi%C3%A8res_-_Christin_-_Tranl%C3%A9.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/06/Valerian_and_Laureline.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/06/Valerian_and_Laureline.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Valérian and Laureline as drawn by Jean-Claude Mézières","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AValerian_and_Laureline.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/76/Mister_Albert.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/76/Mister_Albert.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Mr Albert.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMister_Albert.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5a/Three_shingouz%2C_from_%22The_Ghosts_of_Inverloch%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5a/Three_shingouz%2C_from_%22The_Ghosts_of_Inverloch%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Three shingouz, from \"The Ghosts of Inverloch\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThree_shingouz%2C_from_%22The_Ghosts_of_Inverloch%22.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a6/Valerian_Astroship.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conten